      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the allowed UID ranges will be set for all networks even if the PROFILE_NETWORK_PREFERENCE_ENTERPRISE_BLOCKING is unused. This means that netd pays the cost of uid comparisons in most use cases. Will it better to have a simple check in updateProfileAllowedNetworks which calls mNetd.setNetworkAllowlist with an empty array and returns early when the PROFILE_NETWORK_PREFERENCE_ENTERPRISE_BLOCKING is not selected by any user?",
